  "original_notes": [
    {
      "cell": "H12",
      "text": "To calculate the matrix distance (or the cost to link any 2 points A and B in the graph), we use the mathematical formula:\n\nsqrt( (xA-xB)² + (yA-yB)² )【欧几何距离公式】\n\nThe results are stored in a float variable (in C language) if the costs are real (code 1)\nThe result is multiplied by 100 and truncked to be stored in an integer variable if the costs are interger (code 0)."
    }
